/-!
# Shared infrastructure for the reduction to concrete CFSG

The classification proposition is supplied by the frozen external statement.
It asserts existence of an isomorphism to an explicit model. Transport of
finiteness, simplicity, generation, least subgroup index and the actual outer
automorphism group is proved before quantitative model properties are used.

The alternating family's two-generation and simple-index bounds are proved
without classification; its exceptional degree-six automorphisms are handled
through their action on the two actual order-three conjugacy classes. Twenty
sporadic models have literal generating subsets of size at most two. The
remaining concrete cases are explicitly retained in the reduction theorems.

The literal type-A and Suzuki families now have checked two-generator
and good-Sylow witnesses. Suzuki's original matrix Bruhat decomposition
also supplies its exact order and normalizer intersection.
Suzuki's outer group has order at most the original field exponent,
and its actual least proper index satisfies the required numerical packet.
Shared integral
Serre divided-power and local-nilpotence lemmas support further Lie families;
every displayed root operator now has a checked invertible lift, including
after integral base change. These facts do not assert additive root
parameters, cross-root relations or the uniform finite-type nilpotence bound.
Diagram and field automorphisms now identify the literal graphs for the
ordinary twisted A, D, E6 and triality families. The exceptional long-short
isogenies remain separate.
The original rank-one type-A matrix model also satisfies both actual
least-index bounds, including field orders four and five by the same
argument. The entire type-A family now satisfies both required
simple-index bounds; other family cases remain explicit.
For higher-rank type A the squared-index inequality and the lower bound
`q^r <= ell` are proved on the actual matrix quotient. Transvections are
recognized by Sylow centres, and every automorphism permutes the original
full point-root and hyperplane-root groups. Actual PGL frame alignment
and the frame-stabilizer injection into field automorphisms give the
collineation count. Cancelling the actual inner group then proves
`|Out PSL_n(F)| <= 2*n*|RingAut(F)|` for `n >= 3`, discharging the
numerical adapter's outer premise.
Actual divided-power-stable kernels also support a descended action on
any surjective representation image. A simple source identifies its
projective quotient with the nontrivial projective image; this does not
assume or prove that the image is a named classical group. The six literal
Serre generator relations have a reusable quotient-map constructor.
The concrete symplectic matrices now satisfy those six relations over
the rationals, preserve the original integral lattice, and intertwine
every original root operator after base change. The action on this
actual image has scalar commutant. The full natural symplectic group
identification is proved by the later stabilizer induction.
Its action range is exactly that of the literal elementary matrix group.
When the original projective source is simple, this gives an actual
isomorphism to the elementary group's central quotient; no Lie-algebra
faithfulness or full classical-group generation is assumed.
In characteristic two every original root lift is an involution. Any
nontrivial quotient of an untwisted Serre model consequently has even
cardinality, without a matrix-group recognition hypothesis.
The symplectic realization also supplies a noncentral fourth root of
one in every characteristic, proving even cardinality for all original
simple type-C models. Their entire classifier branch is discharged
from the parity residual, including odd characteristic.
For field order two and every classifier-admissible rank, an explicit
Coxeter word and a disjoint order-three/root word generate the actual
elementary group. Transport through the same projective realization proves
two-generation for the original binary type-C models. Nonbinary type-C
models use a different explicit pair: full long-root extraction, actual
coordinate tori and signed Coxeter propagation recover every original
simple-root parameter. The three-element field has its own checked pair.
Thus every classifier-admissible type-C model is two-generated, and the
entire C branch is removed from the exact generation residual. The same
natural matrices identify with the full form-preserving symplectic group:
the rank-one Gaussian base and the actual hyperbolic-pair stabilizer
prove surjectivity in all ranks. This is a proved theorem, not an input.
The same first-pair stabilizer recurrence and an exact affine-fibre count
now prove the full finite order formula
`|Sp_(2*n)(K)| = q^(n*n) * product_(i=1..n) (q^(2*i)-1)`,
including ranks zero and one, with no published order premise.
The original untransposed type-D model now has the same complete
rational-to-integral image construction, using a shared square-zero
matrix realization. The two fork projections prove a scalar commutant
in every characteristic. Its actual elementary central quotient is
isomorphic to the original simple projective source. A noncentral
chain Weyl word of fourth power one proves even order for the entire
original type-D family, removing all D tags from the parity residual.
An actual generating pair also recovers all original simple roots for
every binary type-D rank at least four. The exact generation residual
omits the binary D tags. The subsequent nonbinary pair uses primitive
root-parameter extraction and signed star propagation; both endpoint
geometries recover the original short roots and Weyl word in the same
subgroup. Every original D model of rank at least four is therefore
two-generated, and all D tags are removed from the exact generation
residual. No full orthogonal-group recognition theorem is assumed.
For the original symplectic model, the actual short-root conjugacy
and a moved natural projective point prove `q <= ell` and
`ell*(q-1) <= q^(2*r)-1`. The natural centre has at most two elements
and is trivial in characteristic two. An injective block-cell chart
counts symmetric parameter pairs exactly. Every symmetric shear belongs
to the actual elementary group. An augmented cell with a two-coordinate
Borel factor proves `ell^2 < |G|` for every admissible original C model,
including characteristic two. Actual elementary words also move every
nonzero natural vector and every hyperbolic partner. Intrinsic abstract
root recognition and the outer bound are proved in the later complete
simple-index packet. In odd characteristic actual Sylow centres
recognize the projective natural roots. In characteristic two the same
normalizer-centre atom construction gives at most three images of the
original root conjugacy family. Its stabilizer acts faithfully on the
original points. Orthogonality yields collineations; the literal PGSp
count and exact field frame stabilizer bound the actual outer group.
The entire original C family consequently satisfies both required
simple-index inequalities and leaves that exact remaining-model predicate.
The actual natural root lines descend injectively to the projective
quotient: a common nonzero fixed vector forces any central scalar
relating two transvections to equal one. Their parameters, cardinalities,
projective labels and conjugation laws are consequently exact.
The natural type-B realization retains the short roots' quadratic
exponential coefficients. The fourth conjugation coefficient is proved
zero on the actual original image before using the source's four-term
root operator. In odd characteristic its scalar commutant and actual
projective image give the original-model comparison. Together with the
characteristic-two root-involution proof, a chain Weyl word proves
even order for every original type-B model. All B tags are removed from
the exact parity residual.
The original G2 Serre model also has a checked rational/integral
representation, obtained by folding the three outer D4 roots. The
short-root polynomial retains its genuine quadratic coefficient. On
the actual representation image a long Weyl word has fourth power one
and is noncentral. Simple projective descent proves even order for
all original simple G2 models. The natural eight-dimensional module
is reducible; the proof uses its actual action image and assumes no
scalar-commutant or named-group recognition assertion. Twisted G2
and other exceptional cases remain explicit in the parity residual.

The soluble-generation extension steps and the bounded binary counting leaf
are also proved here. Importing this file does not replace any outstanding
published input of T1 by an unproved concrete-model assertion.
-/

/-! In characteristic two, restriction of the actual B matrices to their
hyperbolic block is an isomorphism with the literal elementary C group.
The invariant transpose-quadratic form proves its kernel trivial. The
original simple Serre source therefore inherits two-generation, and only
these B tags leave the exact generation residual. The subsequent odd-field
pair uses actual quadratic short roots, a fork torus, scalar filtering
and a cleaned signed Coxeter orbit. The coefficient two is inverted
only in odd characteristic, including field order three. Thus every
original B model of rank at least three is two-generated, and the
entire B branch leaves the exact generation residual. -/

/-! The actual E6/E7/E8 norm-two integer lattices now supply finite,
reduced, irreducible crystallographic root pairings, literal coordinate
bases, and transpose-correct Cartan identities. The six Serre relations
then give representations of the original rational Lie presentations
on their actual Geck matrix spaces. Their literal integral divided-power
matrices and same-image fourth-coefficient cancellation are also proved,
including explicit E6/E7/E8 installers over every coefficient ring.
The actual Weyl word is now noncentral in the same generated image
and has fourth power one in every characteristic. Simple projective
descent proves even order on each original E6/E7/E8 model. Generation
and outer bounds remain separate obligations. -/

/-! The same characteristic-two B image action is now proved faithful
using its actual terminal-root image and nonzero-vector orbit. Centre
quotient functoriality therefore identifies the ORIGINAL B projective
model with natural projective C, and simplicity transfers in that
direction. Both required simple-index bounds hold for these B tags;
only odd-characteristic B remains in that family residual. -/

/-! The generic primitive-input foundations now bound every actual
composition chain by log₂ of its group order. Every subnormal subgroup
of a finite product of nonabelian simple groups is proved to be a literal
coordinate product, and every actual composition chain of that product
has length at most the number of original factors. These facts use no
classification premise; the sharper quantitative primitive inputs remain
separate obligations. -/

/-! The original D models now satisfy the required squared least-index
inequality, an explicit projective-point upper bound, and the stronger
root-star lower bound q^(r-1) <= ell. All are proved through actual matrix
subgroups and the same original central quotient. The D outer-group
bound is still an independent open model obligation. -/

/-! Odd-characteristic B now has the required squared least-index
inequality and explicit lower/upper index bounds on the original model.
The actual elementary centre is proved trivial using both its quadratic
form and determinant, including q=3/rank3. The logarithmic B outer-group
estimate is still open, so these tags remain in that combined residual. -/

/-! The actual primitive-profile foundations now include ordinary rank
addition across the literal kernel, and a same-series composition bound
k + log2|G/S| for a full semisimple socle S=T^k. Affine profiles have the
proved coarse bound (1+floor(log2 n))*log2 n for every composition series
and every subgroup's ordinary rank. The nonaffine normal-rank bound is
2k+log2|G/S| under the explicit simple-factor rank<=2 premise. These
coarse estimates do not assert the sharper retained primitive inputs. -/

/-! Exactly the untwisted E6/E7/E8 tags now leave the parity residual.
The coefficient-one noncentral witness works in characteristic two too,
and is tested on the same original E-generator image. Twisted exceptional
and other remaining models are retained explicitly. -/

/-! The actual raw primitive dichotomy now assembles degree-only coarse
bounds L²+3L for every original composition series, and L²+4L for every
actual normal subgroup's ordinary rank, L=log2(degree). Their only
quantitative inputs are the displayed simple-index/Out and, for rank,
simple-two-generation premises. They do not use the retained primitive
composition or primitive normal-generation inputs. -/

/-! The literal D flag-unitriangular subgroup now has centre exactly
its highest paired-root line, isomorphic to the same additive field;
its fixed vectors are exactly the first natural line. These assertions
hold in every characteristic and use the actual split quadratic form,
not merely its polar form. Odd-characteristic Sylow maximality is now proved for this same subgroup.
The all-characteristic component and good-Sylow continuation is now proved below;
D outer geometry remains separate. -/

/-! For odd B the literal U is now proved Sylow, N(U) is its actual
flag Borel, and Z(U) is exactly the highest long-root field line. Its
conjugate root lines are now intrinsically preserved by every actual
projective automorphism. Each literal line has a well-defined natural
two-plane label, recovered as range(x-I) for a nonidentity root element.
Surjectivity onto all singular planes and the exact projective action on them
are now proved below. Semilinear realization and the outer bound remain open. -/

/-! Those coarse primitive bounds are now uniformly sublinear in degree.
Their first checked applications are the eventual c=1 relative-character
tail and the eventual primitive three-tenths chief-weight tail. They retain
only the displayed simple-group inputs, not the sharp primitive inputs.
No fixed cutoff 34 or45, or coverage below a new cutoff, is asserted. -/

/-! The original untwisted F4 model now has even order in every characteristic.
The proof folds the actual E6 Geck representation, verifies the pinned F4
Cartan relations, and tests a long-root Weyl word on that same image.
Only F4 leaves this parity residual; its generation/Out bounds and the
twisted exceptional cases remain open. -/

/-! The odd-characteristic D Sylow proof retains the final middle 2-plane.
Its actual normalizer action is diagonal or anti-diagonal; a p-power
anti-diagonal element contradicts its determinant one exactly when 2!=0.
This argument makes no characteristic-two component assertion. -/

/-! The actual C defining-characteristic Sylow has a soluble normalizer
and generates with its actual J-conjugate. This good-Sylow datum descends
to the original C projective model and, through the proved characteristic-two
B/C quotient equivalence, to original binary B. Exactly those families
leave the narrowed Aschbacher--Guralnick model callback. Other leaves remain.

The original derived-fixed twisted-E6 projective model now has even order
in every characteristic. At prime two, actual A2 Singer-seven and Weyl-braid
identities put the original positive and negative roots in the derived image;
literal source lifts recover the same noncentral long-root Weyl word.
Only twisted E6 leaves this parity residual; other tags remain explicit.

Odd-B singular-vector normalization is now proved on the same natural
matrix action, in rank at least two. The continuation covers all totally singular two-planes and carries the exact
projective automorphism action. The actual point action is proved below; semilinear/outer reconstruction remains open. -/

/-! The combined good-Sylow callback now removes every original B and D
model as well as A, C and Suzuki. D uses the all-characteristic parity of
three maximal singular-space distances to exclude the last-pair swap
from its actual unipotent normalizer; no order/component premise is used.
B uses the literal product of coordinate flips, with the middle weight
and full quadratic short-root terms retained. Each actual natural Sylow
has a soluble normalizer and generates with the displayed conjugate.
The other model tags remain in the explicit callback, so this is not a
CFSG-only proof of the whole published soluble-generation input. -/

/-! Original odd-B singular points now satisfy the proved incidence-star
axioms for intersecting nonadjacent singular two-planes. Exact same-cone
counts prove the local bridge, and the reconstructed faithful relation
action preserves point orthogonality. The explicit R11 lower count is now
proved on the original residual vectors and installs the actual faithful
projective-group automorphism action in `originalPointAction`. No count
or recognition premise remains in that action. Semilinear realization
and the quantitative outer bound remain open.

Original D singular vector/pair/plane normalization and the intrinsic
root-product adjacency relation are now proved in every characteristic.
Four/six-form joint-fixed vectors lift these particular quotient
commutation/product relations; arbitrary quotient automorphisms are not
lifted. D4 triality and the outer bound remain separate obligations.

For the actual E6/E7/E8 models, positive and negative p-subgroups generate,
giving two conjugate Sylow generators. Their literal torus envelope B is
soluble, contains U+, and normalizes U+; every defining-p element of B
lies in U+. The global containment N_G(U+) <= B is not proved here, so
no exceptional good-Sylow or whole published input is removed. -/


/-! The original odd-B inner action now agrees with its literal matrices on
points and every singular subspace. Actual root words align every full-rank
singular image with the positive coordinate space. On each original singular
subspace of dimension at least three, the reconstructed action has a proved
semilinear projective restriction; this is not yet a whole-polar-space
semilinear theorem. Restricted functionals and opposition rigidity are proved.
The actual rank-one elementary B group has index at most two in the literal
special isometry group, without a named-group recognition input.

For original D in rank at least five, the R11 neighbour gap reconstructs the
faithful original point action over every finite field. Its singular-subspace
extension retains Q=0, not just polar-self-orthogonality in characteristic two.
Local semilinearity on each Q-singular subspace is proved. Rank-four triality
and whole-space semilinearity remain open.

The actual exceptional adjacent collecting word now holds with arbitrary two
parameters over every field, via exact integer polynomial identities. These
local collecting identities do not yet prove global Bruhat decomposition or
the reverse Sylow-normalizer containment. No further public input is removed.
-/


/-! The special-isometry index bound is now proved in EVERY positive
original B rank over an odd finite field. The actual inverse maximal-space
normalization and right-hand parabolic factorization give a one-sided cover;
actual last-pair square words give index at most two. No SO/Omega recognition,
order formula, or unproved elementary normality premise is used. -/
